Package: ssadequacy
Type: Package
Title: Sample Size Adequacy: Joint Power, Precision, Stability and
        Feasibility Planning
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Cansu", "Ergenç Özdaş", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "cansuergenc7@gmail.com",
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4722-0911",
                              affiliation = "Ankara Yıldırım Beyazıt University, cansuergenc@aybu.edu.tr"))
Description: Implements the Sample Size Adequacy (SSA) framework, in which the
    minimum adequate sample size is the smallest N that jointly satisfies
    detectability (power), precision (confidence interval width, optionally
    with assurance; Kelley and Rausch (2006) <doi:10.1037/1082-989X.11.4.363>),
    stability (relative bias) and feasibility (rate of admissible solutions).
    Provides closed-form predictions of the binding criterion based on
    unit-information asymptotics, generalizing Goodman and Berlin (1994)
    <doi:10.7326/0003-4819-121-3-199408010-00008>, a calibrated
    weak-identification law for the admissibility of confirmatory factor
    analysis solutions, and Monte Carlo verification with root finding for
    confirmatory factor analysis (via 'lavaan'), multiple regression and
    one-way ANOVA. Non-normal data are generated with the method of Vale and
    Maurelli (1983) <doi:10.1007/BF02293687>. An interactive 'shiny' planner
    is included.
